WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.000
From 99 dollars to

00:00:01.812 --> 00:00:03.592
250,000

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.242
Early Unix was

00:00:05.053 --> 00:00:06.786
available through inexpensive

00:00:06.598 --> 00:00:07.954
source-code licenses

00:00:08.049 --> 00:00:09.723
because a 1956

00:00:09.535 --> 00:00:10.737
antitrust settlement

00:00:10.596 --> 00:00:11.975
kept AT&T out

00:00:11.787 --> 00:00:12.659
of the commercial

00:00:12.471 --> 00:00:13.614
computer business

00:00:14.134 --> 00:00:15.726
But AT&T's breakup

00:00:15.537 --> 00:00:17.270
in 1984 opened the

00:00:17.082 --> 00:00:17.813
way to sell

00:00:17.625 --> 00:00:18.780
Unix commercially

00:00:18.957 --> 00:00:19.900
and it abruptly

00:00:19.712 --> 00:00:20.631
raised the price

00:00:20.443 --> 00:00:23.851
from 99 dollars to 250,000 dollars

00:00:24.374 --> 00:00:25.494
Berkeley released its

00:00:25.306 --> 00:00:26.590
networking code as

00:00:26.402 --> 00:00:27.510
Net / 1

00:00:27.322 --> 00:00:28.949
in June 1989

00:00:29.103 --> 00:00:30.034
and a completely

00:00:29.846 --> 00:00:31.308
free BSD Unix

00:00:31.261 --> 00:00:32.475
finally shipped in

00:00:32.287 --> 00:00:33.760
June 1991

00:00:34.278 --> 00:00:35.292
Full story on

00:00:35.103 --> 00:00:35.999
the dashboard
